{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"externalID":"Traffluent","title":"Traffluent","roleHeading":"Framework"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests"]},{"title":"Modules","anchor":"Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums"]},{"title":"Testing","anchor":"Testing","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting"]}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event is a value conforming to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" is a value: tracking an event records it as an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord"},{"type":"text","text":", with its timestamp, the caller’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SourceLocation"},{"type":"text","text":" and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"type":"text","text":", as one of the tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"records"},{"type":"text","text":". Delivering is a chain of operators over that sequence: Afluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch(strategy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"},{"type":"text","text":", the default) gathers the records into batches, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" hands each batch to every destination, as a lazy unit of work. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destination"},{"type":"text","text":" is a plain sink, narrowed or transformed by its modifiers: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accepting(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for the consent categories it serves, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"redactingSensitiveValues()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"droppingCallSite()"},{"type":"text","text":". A tracker given a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Consent"},{"type":"text","text":" delivers an event only once the user grants its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ConsentCategory"},{"type":"text","text":", holding it while undecided and dropping it when denied. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"type":"text","text":" only queues an event, from any thread; a worker the tracker owns, never on the main actor, does the rest. A tracker given a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":" writes each record to disk as its worker reaches it and delivers what an earlier run left first. A property whose valid values are narrower than its type is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refined"},{"type":"text","text":" value, which satisfies its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refinement"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Constraint"},{"type":"text","text":"s from the moment it is made, or carries constraints declared with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Constrained"},{"type":"text","text":"; the tracker’s worker rejects an event that breaks one before anything else, reporting each as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RejectionReport"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rejectionReports"},{"type":"text","text":". On Apple platforms, SwiftUI views read the tracker from the environment and track what they do with view modifiers, and a screen’s events carry its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenKey"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking"},{"type":"text","text":"). UIKit views and view controllers inherit it as a trait, the same value as SwiftUI’s, set on a window scene ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking"},{"type":"text","text":"), and AppKit views find it up their responder chain ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking"},{"type":"text","text":"); a control’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks an event through the tracker found when its action fires, so each scene or window can have its own. Screen views can track themselves once a window scene or window turns it on with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreensAutomatically"},{"type":"text","text":", which tracks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenViewed"},{"type":"text","text":" as each screen’s view controller appears, without swizzling ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking"},{"type":"text","text":"), and UIKit controls once a window scene turns it on with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackControlsAutomatically"},{"type":"text","text":", which tracks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ControlActivated"},{"type":"text","text":" as a touch activates each control named by its accessibility identifier ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking"},{"type":"text","text":"). On every platform, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackLifecycle"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks the app’s installs, updates, opens, moves to the background and terminations, and makes the tracker’s records durable as it leaves the foreground ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking"},{"type":"text","text":"). A tracker given the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions"},{"type":"text","text":" enricher stamps every event with its session’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", a random identifier held in memory only, and starts a new session after a timeout of inactivity, tracking "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionEnded"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionStarted"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions"},{"type":"text","text":"). A tracker given "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler"},{"type":"text","text":"s keeps a seeded fraction of the events they apply to, event by event, or whole sessions with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)"},{"type":"text","text":", dropping the rest on its worker before they are held, written or delivered, reporting each drop as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SamplingDropReport"},{"type":"text","text":" and stamping each kept record with its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SampleRateKey"},{"type":"text","text":". The standard enrichers, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.application()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"operatingSystem()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vendorIdentifier()"},{"type":"text","text":", stamp every event with the app, device, operating system, locale, network connection and the platform’s identifier for vendor, each under a typed key, the static ones read once ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" imports every module but "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", a product of its own for apps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that already use GRDB; "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" macro derives an event’s conformances"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and schema from its declaration and which alone builds swift-syntax; "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exports those schemas as a JSON Schema tracking plan and checks the events against a committed one;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which runs that check from an app’s tests; and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withRecordingTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" gives a test’s body a fresh tracker and returns what it tracked. Each module also has its own documentation and can be imported on its own."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Traffluent","","struct SignedUp: Event {","    var plan: String","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: ConsoleDestination())","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()"]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"},"references":{"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros":{"url":"\/documentation\/eventmacros","abstract":[],"title":"EventMacros","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros"},"doc://LoggingDestinations/documentation/LoggingDestinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/loggingdestinations","abstract":[],"title":"LoggingDestinations","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations"},"doc://GRDBPersistence/documentation/GRDBPersistence":{"url":"\/documentation\/grdbpersistence","abstract":[],"title":"GRDBPersistence","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/IdentifyingPeople":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/identifyingpeople","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent knows people only by a pseudonymous session. An identifier that outlives one is yours to add, store, reset and gate with consent."}],"title":"Identifying People"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"title":"Traffluent"},"doc://AutomaticControlTracking/documentation/AutomaticControlTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/automaticcontroltracking","abstract":[],"title":"AutomaticControlTracking","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking"},"doc://SwiftUITracking/documentation/SwiftUITracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","abstract":[],"title":"SwiftUITracking","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking"},"doc://Checksums/documentation/Checksums":{"url":"\/documentation\/checksums","abstract":[],"title":"Checksums","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums"},"doc://TrackingPlanTesting/documentation/TrackingPlanTesting":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplantesting","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"TrackingPlanTesting"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"TrackingPlans"},"doc://AppKitTracking/documentation/AppKitTracking":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","url":"\/documentation\/appkittracking","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"AppKitTracking"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PrivacyManifests":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels.","type":"text"}],"title":"Privacy Manifests"},"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/destinations","abstract":[],"title":"Destinations","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence","abstract":[],"title":"Persistence","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"},"doc://TrackerTesting/documentation/TrackerTesting":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/trackertesting","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","abstract":[],"type":"topic","title":"TrackerTesting"},"doc://UIKitTracking/documentation/UIKitTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/uikittracking","abstract":[],"title":"UIKitTracking","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events":{"url":"\/documentation\/events","abstract":[],"title":"Events","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events"},"doc://StandardContext/documentation/StandardContext":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","url":"\/documentation\/standardcontext","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"StandardContext"},"doc://AutomaticScreenTracking/documentation/AutomaticScreenTracking":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","url":"\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"AutomaticScreenTracking"},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","url":"\/documentation\/trackers","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"Trackers"},"doc://Sessions/documentation/Sessions":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/sessions","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"Sessions"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"HTTPDestinations"},"doc://LifecycleTracking/documentation/LifecycleTracking":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","url":"\/documentation\/lifecycletracking","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"LifecycleTracking"},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"TracingDestinations"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it."}],"title":"Changing an Event"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/WhatGoesWhere":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/whatgoeswhere","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Four signals, four jobs. Decide which one a fact belongs to before you write the line that records it.","type":"text"}],"title":"Logging, Tracing, Metrics and Analytics"}}}